id: SCA-025
title: GitHub Actions workflow with broad write permissions
category: supply-chain
severity: info
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .yml .yaml
  exclude_paths: test/ node_modules/ .git/ vendor/
  content_contains: permissions
patterns:
  - regex: permissions:\s*write-all
    message: write-all gives every step (including third-party actions) ability to push code, create releases, or publish packages.
  - regex: contents:\s*write
    message: contents write permission allows steps to push code or create releases — use least-privilege.
  - regex: packages:\s*write
    message: packages write permission allows steps to publish packages — use least-privilege.
fix: Use least-privilege permissions. Set permissions read-all at workflow level and grant write only to specific jobs that need it.
